                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm assuming this was unintentional to switch back?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-nvl32-obmc/conf/machine/nvl32-obmc.conf",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "this was intentional, as we're still waiting for feedback/merge on the newest revision of the patch series to u-boot. What was unintentional was the previous patch changing it to the msx4 which isn't merged, but we override it below on line 7, so this goof has no effect. I'm going to put up a new revision that just gets rid of this line. We can still boot and function fine without the dt (with this patch), just that specific hardware pieces aren't accurate and we're relying on this u-boot env hack to disable FMC_WDT2"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-nvl32-obmc/conf/machine/nvl32-obmc.conf",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
